  "title": "Illusion of Agency over Electrically-Actuated Movements",
  "description": "This dataset contains electroencephalography (EEG) recordings from a study investigating the illusion of agency over electrically-actuated bodily movements. The research examines how individuals perceive control over movements induced via electrical muscle stimulation, contributing to the understanding of the sense of agency in human-computer interaction and body perception. Data were collected from human participants and organized according to the Brain Imaging Data Structure (BIDS) standard.",
